1
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:07,079
It's not completely hopeless.

2
00:01:08,719 --> 00:01:09,319
If that doesn't work,

3
00:01:10,959 --> 00:01:12,280
we can try Chinese medicine again.

4
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:14,920
Don't bother.

5
00:01:18,599 --> 00:01:20,280
I know my own body.

6
00:01:22,799 --> 00:01:23,599
Honey...

7
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:26,319
I can't bear to let go.

8
00:01:27,319 --> 00:01:29,280
He's the reason I can't go on living.

9
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:34,680
Then we might as well die together.

10
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:42,000
Even if I die, I'll take him down with me.

11
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:50,719
What?

12
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:52,959
You scared?

13
00:02:03,719 --> 00:02:04,840
If we're going to rot,

14
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:07,719
then let's all rot to the core.

15
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:12,400
Worst case, we all go down together.

16
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,599
Later on,

17
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,199
my wife and I kept our eyes on him

18
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:29,879
and his wife.

19
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,479
Seeing how happy his family was,

20
00:02:36,159 --> 00:02:37,759
carrying his daughter while grocery shopping,

21
00:02:39,919 --> 00:02:41,479
teaching his son to fly a kite...

22
00:02:47,199 --> 00:02:48,560
We felt like

23
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:51,199
the two of them were putting on a show for us.

24
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:53,560
Taunting us.

25
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,439
So we bought knives

26
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,280
and picked a date,

27
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:07,560
waiting for him and his wife to get off work

28
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:09,680
and pick up the kids together.

29
00:03:11,199 --> 00:03:12,000
A big crowd,

30
00:03:12,719 --> 00:03:13,520
bustling.

31
00:03:15,479 --> 00:03:17,680
We wanted them, in front of everyone,

32
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,039
to be punished.

33
00:03:21,599 --> 00:03:22,960
We stabbed Wang Tao first,

34
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:25,840
then slashed his wife.

35
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:29,639
When my wife smashed his daughter's head with a brick,

36
00:03:29,639 --> 00:03:31,120
just as I stepped up to finish her off,

37
00:03:31,159 --> 00:03:31,960
I noticed...

38
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:34,319
I noticed...

39
00:03:35,719 --> 00:03:37,039
I noticed his son wasn't there.

40
00:03:41,719 --> 00:03:42,599
What a pity.

41
00:03:45,759 --> 00:03:46,639
Such a pity.

42
00:03:48,199 --> 00:03:49,520
The two of us acted too rashly.

43
00:03:50,639 --> 00:03:51,680
Didn't time it right.

44
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,800
Why slaughter his whole family?

45
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:56,759
Why?

46
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,879
What did a six-year-old kid

47
00:03:59,879 --> 00:04:01,560
have to do with your dirty business?

48
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,080
You animals!

49
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,240
If Wang Tao were still alive,

50
00:04:17,519 --> 00:04:18,680
do you think

51
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:21,160
he'd regret it?

52
00:04:22,639 --> 00:04:24,120
I gave him a chance.

53
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,519
If he had just given me that 100,000 yuan,

54
00:04:26,519 --> 00:04:27,639
wouldn't that have been the end of it?

55
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:30,040
Did it really have to come to this?

56
00:04:31,639 --> 00:04:32,480
Serves him right.

57
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:34,079
Serves him right.

58
00:05:33,199 --> 00:05:34,560
As for the human heart,

59
00:05:34,879 --> 00:05:36,319
it's even harder to crack

60
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,040
than many cold cases.

61
00:05:40,279 --> 00:05:42,399
The more cases we handle,

62
00:05:42,519 --> 00:05:43,560
and the deeper we dig,

63
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:45,079
the more we realize

64
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:46,959
there's not just

65
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,600
black and white.

66
00:05:49,199 --> 00:05:50,319
There are also many

67
00:05:50,319 --> 00:05:51,759
shades we can't fathom.

68
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:52,959
Many of the answers,

69
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:54,839
the law can give you.

70
00:05:56,399 --> 00:05:57,680
But when it comes to the human heart,

71
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:01,199
that requires our understanding

72
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:03,160
and our own judgment.

73
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:18,720
Don't do anything reckless.

74
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:19,319
Stay calm.

75
00:06:19,319 --> 00:06:20,040
Stay back! Step back!

76
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:21,600
Back off!

77
00:06:21,839 --> 00:06:22,680
Let the kid go.

78
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:23,240
Stay back!

79
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,120
Let go of the kid!

80
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,079
Back off! Back off!

81
00:06:25,079 --> 00:06:25,600
Okay, I'm backing off.

82
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:26,279
Step back!

83
00:06:26,279 --> 00:06:26,879
I'm stepping back.

84
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,000
I want a car!

85
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:29,800
Just wait.

86
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:30,759
Give me the radio.

87
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,759
Get a car ready. Arrange a car now.

88
00:06:35,079 --> 00:06:35,920
Copy that, Captain Meng.

89
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:37,360
Happy now?

90
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:39,639
Have them drive it downstairs!

91
00:06:39,639 --> 00:06:40,279
Right downstairs!

92
00:06:40,279 --> 00:06:41,079
All right, all right.

93
00:06:41,079 --> 00:06:42,079
Bring it downstairs.

94
00:06:42,079 --> 00:06:43,199
Drive the car downstairs.

95
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Copy, Captain Meng.

96
00:06:45,319 --> 00:06:47,199
Loosen your grip on the kid.

97
00:06:47,279 --> 00:06:48,800
Don't point that gun at me!

98
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:50,360
Stop pointing that gun at me!

99
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,000
Don't push me!

100
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,079
Don't push me!

101
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:55,800
You don't need to be so nervous.

102
00:06:56,079 --> 00:06:56,920
When is the car getting here?

103
00:06:57,399 --> 00:06:58,319
Take it easy.

104
00:06:58,319 --> 00:06:59,319
When's the car getting here?

105
00:06:59,319 --> 00:07:00,240
Hurry up!

106
00:07:00,439 --> 00:07:01,439
Stay back!

107
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:02,600
It's on the way.

108
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:03,439
Stay right there! Don't move!

109
00:07:03,879 --> 00:07:04,600
Don't come any closer!

110
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,839
Listen to me, let's talk this out.

111
00:07:05,959 --> 00:07:07,120
No way! No!

112
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,319
Don't... the kid...

113
00:07:08,319 --> 00:07:09,439
Don't scare the kid.

114
00:07:09,439 --> 00:07:10,360
Shut up!

115
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:12,120
Wait, no, don't, don't!

116
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:12,920
Look at what you're doing.

117
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:13,839
Why take it out on her?

118
00:07:13,839 --> 00:07:14,319
No, between the two of us—

119
00:07:14,319 --> 00:07:15,040
Stay back!

120
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:15,600
We can talk this through—

121
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:16,199
Don't come any closer!

122
00:07:16,199 --> 00:07:16,759
Listen to me.

123
00:07:16,759 --> 00:07:17,800
Let me talk to you.

124
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:18,920
I'll kill you, believe me!

125
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:19,959
No, hey, no, no, no.

126
00:07:19,959 --> 00:07:21,560
Come on, look at you...

127
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:22,600
There's no point in doing this.

128
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:22,920
Back off!

129
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:23,639
We're getting it arranged!

130
00:07:23,639 --> 00:07:24,600
We're giving you everything you want!

131
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,800
And you're still pulling this?

132
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:27,839
Come on, don't you think?

133
00:07:28,199 --> 00:07:28,720
All right, all right.

134
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:31,160
Don't cry, don't cry, it's okay.

135
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,480
Just let the kid—

136
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:33,360
Let go of the kid.

137
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:34,920
Just get me the car!

138
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:35,680
Get me that car!

139
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:36,480
Okay, okay, okay.

140
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:41,000
Quick, quick! Secure the scene!

141
00:07:43,279 --> 00:07:44,480
It's okay, sweetheart, you're safe.

142
00:07:45,439 --> 00:07:45,879
Let's go.

143
00:08:42,759 --> 00:08:44,039
The left leg is an old injury.

144
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:45,720
Fractured lower leg below the knee.

145
00:08:46,519 --> 00:08:47,360
Preliminary findings show

146
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:48,960
he's been dead for over ten days.

147
00:08:49,159 --> 00:08:51,000
This was found on the body.

148
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,080
He's from out of town.

149
00:09:02,879 --> 00:09:03,720
He Yiqiang.

150
00:09:07,159 --> 00:09:07,840
Look into him.

151
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:24,919
Stop, stop, stop.

152
00:09:27,679 --> 00:09:29,240
Can you zoom in on this?

153
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:30,039
Sure.

154
00:09:33,519 --> 00:09:34,320
Stop.

155
00:09:40,759 --> 00:09:42,360
Who could this man be?

156
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:46,200
Thank you.

157
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:47,919
Thanks.

158
00:10:14,879 --> 00:10:15,679
Who is it?

159
00:10:19,399 --> 00:10:20,120
Who are you looking for?

160
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:22,080
You're Han Yan, right?

161
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,639
We're investigating a case.

162
00:10:27,039 --> 00:10:27,879
We need your cooperation.

163
00:10:29,759 --> 00:10:30,120
Come on in.

164
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:35,960
Have a seat.

165
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:41,799
What's this all about?

166
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:47,799
Take a look at this.

167
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:49,320
Is this your husband?

168
00:10:54,519 --> 00:10:55,320
Yes.

169
00:10:55,759 --> 00:10:57,440
Who's the injured man?

170
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:00,440
His name is He Yiqiang.

171
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,600
I met him when I was working.

172
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:03,840
You met him at work?

173
00:11:06,879 --> 00:11:08,120
Between him and you two,

174
00:11:09,039 --> 00:11:09,480
what exactly is

175
00:11:10,039 --> 00:11:10,840
the relationship?

176
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:12,679
Nothing really.

177
00:11:12,799 --> 00:11:13,639
It's just that

178
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:16,159
he broke his leg at a construction site,

179
00:11:16,639 --> 00:11:18,240
and had no family or relatives around here.

180
00:11:18,519 --> 00:11:20,799
So my husband and I just helped him out,

181
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,519
waiting until he got better.

182
00:11:22,879 --> 00:11:23,879
So he got injured,

183
00:11:25,279 --> 00:11:27,240
and you and your husband took care of him?

184
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,559
Where's your husband?

185
00:11:34,039 --> 00:11:35,159
Working at the fish pond.

186
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:38,720
Then where is

187
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:40,600
He Yiqiang now?

188
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:42,360
I don't know.

189
00:11:43,279 --> 00:11:44,320
My husband said

190
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:46,000
his family picked him up.

191
00:11:46,519 --> 00:11:47,879
I don't know where he is.

192
00:11:48,639 --> 00:11:49,440
What's wrong?

193
00:11:50,399 --> 00:11:52,360
Are you sure his family picked him up?

194
00:11:54,799 --> 00:11:56,279
Do you believe what your husband said?

195
00:11:58,240 --> 00:11:59,360
How could that be a lie?

196
00:12:11,919 --> 00:12:12,399
Take a look.

197
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,080
He's dead.

198
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:30,279
I didn't know.

199
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:31,919
I had no idea.

200
00:12:32,559 --> 00:12:33,399
Sit down first.

201
00:12:34,279 --> 00:12:35,559
We believe you didn't know.

202
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:37,600
But you have to tell us

203
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:38,960
everything you know, in full detail.

204
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,679
You can't hold anything back.

205
00:12:40,919 --> 00:12:42,000
Do you understand?

206
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,399
No wonder.

207
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:49,600
He said it was all in the past.

208
00:13:31,039 --> 00:13:33,279
Hustle up and get to work!

209
00:14:19,799 --> 00:14:20,480
Miss.

210
00:14:21,399 --> 00:14:22,919
Eating alone is no fun.

211
00:14:22,919 --> 00:14:24,000
Let's get something flavorful.

212
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:37,559
Thanks.

213
00:14:53,039 --> 00:14:54,159
You walked so fast,

214
00:14:54,399 --> 00:14:55,480
I could barely catch up.

215
00:14:55,759 --> 00:14:56,639
What are you doing?

216
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:58,720
I bought you some hot...

217
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,080
roast duck rice.

218
00:15:00,799 --> 00:15:03,279
You can't just eat greens all the time.

219
00:15:03,279 --> 00:15:04,240
You need to eat some meat.

220
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,120
I don't want it.

221
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:07,360
Come on, how can you just eat greens?

222
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:08,440
It's bad for your health.

223
00:15:08,559 --> 00:15:09,639
You gotta eat some meat

224
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:12,120
to keep looking prettier and prettier.

225
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:13,000
Have you eaten?

226
00:15:13,039 --> 00:15:13,840
Neither have I.

227
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:18,799
Qiangzi.

228
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:21,320
Stop coming to see me all the time.

229
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:23,080
I have a family.

230
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,320
I have a husband.

231
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,480
I don't care about that.

232
00:15:26,919 --> 00:15:28,720
As for me, well,

233
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,000
my standards are real low.

234
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,559
I don't have any ulterior motives.

235
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:33,639
Just being able to sit with you every day,

236
00:15:33,639 --> 00:15:34,279
sit a little longer,

237
00:15:34,279 --> 00:15:35,600
chat and have a meal,

238
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:37,159
and then

239
00:15:37,759 --> 00:15:38,720
look at the stars.

240
00:15:39,639 --> 00:15:41,240
Though there aren't many stars tonight,

241
00:15:42,159 --> 00:15:43,159
you get the idea.

242
00:15:43,159 --> 00:15:44,200
I don't know why,

243
00:15:44,639 --> 00:15:46,200
but seeing you feels different from anyone else.

244
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:46,919
Do you think the two of us...

245
00:15:46,919 --> 00:15:48,759
were connected in a past life?

246
00:15:49,559 --> 00:15:50,879
Maybe we were husband and wife.

247
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:53,480
Maybe we didn't finish the Broth of Oblivion,

248
00:15:53,559 --> 00:15:54,120
and then

249
00:15:54,559 --> 00:15:55,399
we met again.

250
00:15:59,399 --> 00:16:00,240
Let me tell you, Yan'er,

251
00:16:00,639 --> 00:16:02,320
I'm so thrilled you could come.

252
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:04,519
I haven't been this happy in years.

253
00:16:04,639 --> 00:16:06,799
Even though our setup today

254
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:08,519
is definitely a bit shabby,

255
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:09,799
you can tell, right?

256
00:16:09,799 --> 00:16:11,200
I also carefully

257
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:13,080
put up these fairy lights,

258
00:16:13,399 --> 00:16:13,879
and these...

259
00:16:14,639 --> 00:16:16,960
little New Year blessing signs for the vibe.

260
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,480
The fireworks they set off are wasted on them.

261
00:16:18,799 --> 00:16:20,200
Them... us... them...

262
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,600
We're the blessed ones.

263
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:23,159
They're setting them off for us.

264
00:16:24,399 --> 00:16:25,159
Look at this.

265
00:16:25,679 --> 00:16:27,240
Last time I was on a job,

266
00:16:27,279 --> 00:16:28,440
that boss of mine

267
00:16:28,440 --> 00:16:30,000
praised me for doing good work,

268
00:16:30,039 --> 00:16:31,120
and rewarded me with a bottle of liquor.

269
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:31,679
Good stuff.

270
00:16:31,679 --> 00:16:33,279
You can't even buy this in stores.

271
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:34,519
Since it's New Year's...

272
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:35,879
I don't drink.

273
00:16:35,879 --> 00:16:37,120
Come on, listen to me.

274
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:38,879
Have just a little. It has no kick later.

275
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:39,919
Just a tiny bit, then.

276
00:16:39,919 --> 00:16:40,840
Alright, alright, alright.

277
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,840
However much you say.

278
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:49,159
Here, Yan'er.

279
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:54,279
Happy New Year.

280
00:16:54,399 --> 00:16:55,200
Happy New Year.

281
00:16:55,559 --> 00:16:56,440
Happy New Year.

282
00:17:03,759 --> 00:17:05,519
Come on, try this.

283
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:06,559
I'm not much of a cook,

284
00:17:06,559 --> 00:17:08,240
but this is a dish from back home.

285
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,640
Northeastern Chinese stew.

286
00:17:09,839 --> 00:17:10,480
Try it.

287
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:11,519
I'm having some.

288
00:17:11,519 --> 00:17:13,440
Have some! Don't be shy, make yourself at home.

289
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:18,319
It's delicious.

290
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,079
Have another glass.

291
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:24,920
Good things come in pairs.

292
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:29,240
Yan'er,

293
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:30,839
let me toast you again.

294
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:34,519
I'm not good with words,

295
00:17:34,519 --> 00:17:35,680
It's all in this drink.

296
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:36,960
May you make good money,

297
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:38,519
and may everything go your way.

298
00:17:43,359 --> 00:17:44,319
I'm so happy.

299
00:17:44,799 --> 00:17:45,440
Really.

300
00:17:46,119 --> 00:17:47,119
This is...

301
00:17:47,359 --> 00:17:48,839
probably in my whole life,

302
00:17:49,119 --> 00:17:50,799
the happiest New Year I've ever had.

303
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:54,319
You can't imagine how I feel.

304
00:17:56,319 --> 00:17:56,920
Cheers.

305
00:17:56,920 --> 00:17:58,119
Just relax.

306
00:18:00,119 --> 00:18:00,720
What is there to say?

307
00:18:00,759 --> 00:18:01,640
May everything go smoothly.

308
00:18:01,759 --> 00:18:02,640
All right.

309
00:18:08,839 --> 00:18:09,519
Drink as much as you want.

310
00:18:09,519 --> 00:18:10,599
Let me tell you, Yan'er,

311
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:11,720
don't worry about anything.

312
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:13,720
If you want me to take you back,

313
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:14,799
I'll take you back.

314
00:18:14,799 --> 00:18:15,960
If you don't mind staying,

315
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,079
I have room here.

316
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:17,640
Just drink freely.

317
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:18,759
Come on, Qiangzi.

318
00:18:19,079 --> 00:18:20,000
Keep drinking.

319
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:26,519
This liquor is good.

320
00:18:26,519 --> 00:18:27,839
It doesn't really...

321
00:18:27,839 --> 00:18:28,880
It doesn't feel that harsh.

322
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,160
Right, it doesn't have a kick.

323
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:32,000
And it tastes really good.

324
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,519
Mainly, you won't get a headache tomorrow.

325
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:35,359
You usually can't even buy this liquor.

326
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:36,400
Even if you drink too much,

327
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:37,440
you can sleep—sleep in the bed.

328
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,319
I'll take the sofa, no problem.

329
00:18:38,319 --> 00:18:38,839
Come on.

330
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Nothing else will happen.

331
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:40,920
Let's keep drinking.
